1
00:01:16,467 --> 00:01:18,774
"[By Haircut 100 playing]"

2
00:01:21,994 --> 00:01:24,689
♪ Boy meets girl... ♪

3
00:01:24,693 --> 00:01:26,216
Yeah! Come on!

4
00:01:31,221 --> 00:01:32,784
And don't puke on the judges.

5
00:01:32,788 --> 00:01:35,091
Whatever you do, Bela,
don't puke on the judges!

6
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:36,226
Knock, knock.

7
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:38,398
Mommy!

8
00:01:38,402 --> 00:01:39,965
-Hi.
-Hey, love.

9
00:01:39,969 --> 00:01:41,358
Hey.

10
00:01:41,362 --> 00:01:43,795
This doesn't look like
bedtime to me.

11
00:01:43,799 --> 00:01:45,710
Yes, it does.
You're just never here.

12
00:01:45,714 --> 00:01:47,407
I'm never here? Is that right?

13
00:01:47,411 --> 00:01:48,887
Get in bed. Get off.
...DADDO: Come on.

14
00:01:48,891 --> 00:01:50,628
Mom's right, Dancing Queen.

15
00:01:50,632 --> 00:01:53,457
-Dive in there.
-Wait, I need Vulchy.

16
00:01:53,461 --> 00:01:54,806
But you have Teddy. Come on.

17
00:01:54,810 --> 00:01:56,547
Really?

18
00:01:56,551 --> 00:01:58,766
Ugh. Are you sure? For bed?

19
00:01:58,770 --> 00:02:00,942
Vulchy's nice.

20
00:02:00,946 --> 00:02:02,640
The lady at the zoo said
vultures only eat

21
00:02:02,644 --> 00:02:04,685
stuff that's already dead.

22
00:02:04,689 --> 00:02:06,517
All right, baby.

23
00:02:11,783 --> 00:02:13,437
-Love you.
-Love you.

24
00:02:14,873 --> 00:02:16,741
Get some sleep.

25
00:02:16,745 --> 00:02:18,221
-Night night.
-Okay.

26
00:02:18,225 --> 00:02:19,874
You want the door open?

27
00:02:19,878 --> 00:02:22,007
-A little bit.
-Okay.

28
00:02:22,011 --> 00:02:24,401
Night, Mommy. Night, Daddo.

29
00:02:24,405 --> 00:02:25,883
Night night.

30
00:02:33,022 --> 00:02:34,893
Good night, Other Mommy.

31
00:02:38,201 --> 00:02:40,765
I'm not sleepy yet.

32
00:02:40,769 --> 00:02:42,900
Can I keep playing with you?

33
00:02:54,783 --> 00:02:56,697
Other Mommy?

34
00:04:01,371 --> 00:04:03,978
<i>Hello and good morning.</i>

35
00:04:03,982 --> 00:04:08,204
My name is Isabela Martin.

36
00:04:11,468 --> 00:04:13,249
And...

37
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:16,646
this is "The Story of Me."

38
00:04:18,693 --> 00:04:20,691
I'm seven years old.

39
00:04:20,695 --> 00:04:24,303
I live with my mommy and Daddo,

40
00:04:24,307 --> 00:04:27,393
Russell Martin and Ursula Martin.

41
00:04:27,397 --> 00:04:30,222
We are a very happy family.

42
00:04:30,226 --> 00:04:31,702
Louder. Louder.

43
00:04:31,706 --> 00:04:33,312
We can't hear you.

44
00:04:33,316 --> 00:04:35,793
Why's she standing so weird?

45
00:04:35,719 --> 00:04:40,891
My hobbies are dancing, books, and animals.

46
00:04:42,559 --> 00:04:43,518
Glasses look good, Mom.

47
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,200
Can I have a snack?
I'm hungry.

48
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:51,000
<i>Only if you brush your teeth after.</i>

49
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,100
Deal.

50
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Maya, phone!

51
00:04:58,100 --> 00:04:59,200
Who is it?

52
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:03,000
It's your dad. He's late again.

53
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:06,400
Tell him I'm not happy.
I mean it.

54
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:09,100
You can tell him yourself.

55
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,300
Fine. I will.

56
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:13,300
[Door slams]

57
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:17,200
Somebody's in a mood.

58
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:20,100
I'm always in a mood.

59
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,500
Good night, everybody.

60
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
See you in the morning.

